<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30821" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἱᾰμενή</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰᾰμενή</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a river-side pasture, meadow</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν εἱαμενῇ ἕλεος</span> in a marshy
				<i>meadow</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.483
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λειμῶνες ὑπόδροσοι εἱαμεναί τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					25.16
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Dian.</u>
				193
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.1202
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Euph.
				138
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἱαμενὴ δὲ καὶ οὐ βυθός ἐστι
				θαλάσσης</span>, of a <i>shallow creek</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dem.Bith.
				4.5
			</span></i> (prob. a participial form): cf. also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰαμένον:</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νήνεμον, κοῖλον, βοτανώδη</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
